>> title: Texas Sheet Cake
>> category: Cakes & Loaves
>> tags: chocolate, sheet cake, buttermilk, oven
>> servings: 24
>> time: 45 min
>> step.7: whisk, then stir in the pecans

Grease a #13x18-in sheet pan{}.

Preheat the #oven{} to 350°F (175°C).

Boil @unsalted butter{1%cup}(225 g), @water{1%cup}(240 mL), @unsweetened cocoa powder{1/4%cup}(25 g).

Whisk @all-purpose flour{2%cup}(250 g), @granulated sugar{2%cup}(400 g), @baking soda{1%tsp}(6 g), @table salt{1/2%tsp}(3 g) into @&(~1)cocoa mixture{}.

Whisk @eggs{2%large}, @buttermilk{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL) into @&(~1)batter{}.

Bake @&(~1)batter{} at 350°F for ~{20%min}.

Whisk @salted butter{1/2%cup}(115 g; melted), @unsweetened cocoa powder{3%Tbs}(18 g), @whole milk{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @powdered sugar{3%cup}(340 g), then stir in @chopped pecans{1%cup}(110 g; toasted).

Pour @&(~1)icing{} over @&(6)warm cake{}.
